    "body": "I looked at this again today in light of https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/59864 and the specification doesn't really have \"creation time\" as a concept, so this is just broken.\n\nThe parser first creates the element and then appends the attributes. So when the element is created the `muted` attribute is always missing.\n\nCloning first clones the element and then clones the attributes. So when the clone is created the `muted` attribute is always missing.\n\nThis would require some \"element is created\" callback or \"attribute modification reason\" (this is what WebKit has available) but either of those introduce the risk of more attributes introducing undesirable APIs.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4212805966/reactions",
