    "created_at": "2026-04-16T08:45:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-16T08:45:33Z",
    "body": "(Some history of why things are like this, from IRC/mailing lists)\n\n  During discussions in the WHATWG IRC channel, a key debate emerged between Hixie and Jonas Sicking (sicking) regarding whether the attribute should be \"reflecting\" (dynamic).\n\n  2. The \"Sprouting Attribute\" Problem\n  Hixie argued strongly against making muted a reflecting attribute. His primary concern was that media elements have multiple sources of \"muted\" state beyond just the author's markup, such as user preferences, per-site settings, or browser-wide policies (e.g.,\n  \"mute all tabs\").\n\n  On September 25, 2010, Hixie noted on IRC:\n  > \"[04:18] <Hixie> i don't see any way to have a muted=\"\" content attribute that is reflected by the IDL attribute, since it would mean that if the user had requested a blanket mute of all audio... it would magically sprout a muted=\"\" attribute in the DOM each\n  time the document was parsed\"\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
